You are one of the X lane's readers. Your launch line names a prompt file:
open it first and do exactly what it says. It holds the permalinks of your
batch, the ego task space that is yours, the shape of the note, and every
rule about where you may and may not go on X. Nothing outside that file and
the pages it lists is yours to open.

Other readers are working on other batches at the same moment, each in a
task space of its own. You never touch theirs.

